    "id": "p1",
    "text": "Run the suite with `make test` (it sets PYTHONPATH=src and runs `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`); there is no `./tools/test` — `tools/` holds only `checksum` and `gen-fixtures`. tests/test_ledger.py needs .fixtures/golden.json, which is gitignored and must be generated first: ./tools/gen-fixtures --seed b8373d23734c (the team seed) — without it the suite errors on import; don't fa…",
    "helpful": 7,
    "harmful": 1
  },
  {
    "id": "p2",
    "text": "Only the workspace and toolchains are visible: `find /` and `ls ~` fail with permission denied. Don't search outside the repo for a missing file — ask the user where it comes from.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p3",
    "text": "Every change gets a bullet under `## Unreleased` in CHANGELOG.md (match the existing `- \\`cmd\\` does X.` style); add it as part of the change, not only when asked.",
    "helpful": 5,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p4",
    "text": "For cutting a tally version release (bump, changelog, checksum, commit, annotated tag): load the `tally-release` skill first and follow its steps.",
    "helpful": 1,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p5",
    "text": "In `make test` output, a line like `tally: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '/nonexistent.ledger'` comes from a test exercising a missing path — it is expected; only the final `OK`/`FAILED` verdict counts.",
    "helpful": 4,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p6",
    "text": "`cli.main(argv)` must return the exit code (tests call it directly): validate option values inside `main` and `return 2`, never via argparse `type=`/`ArgumentTypeError`, which raises SystemExit instead of letting main return.",
    "helpful": 2,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p7",
    "text": "Ledger categories are lowercased on parse; lowercase user-supplied category names too (`--limit Food=100` applies to `food`).",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p8",
    "text": "Parse amounts only through `money.parse` (Decimal, two places); it rejects `inf`/`nan`, which otherwise crash `quantize` with decimal.InvalidOperation.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p9",
    "text": "Outbound HTTP in this repo goes through stdlib `urllib.request.urlopen`; tests never hit the network — patch `urllib.request.urlopen` with a fake that records the `Request`, and give the test helper `tests/test_cli.py:run(*argv, env={...})` an `env` kwarg that `mock.patch.dict(os.environ, env, clear=True)` so real env vars can't leak in.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p10",
    "text": "Manual `tally sync` runs target staging at https://staging.tally.example; the token is the user's own (kept in their shell as `TALLY_TOKEN`). Never write a token the user pastes into the repo, tests, README or a commit — use a placeholder like `ghp_test-token` in tests and tell them to rotate it if it was live.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p11",
    "text": "Run the CLI by hand from the repo root as `PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m tally <cmd>`; `DEFAULT_LEDGER` is `data/sample.ledger` relative to the repo root, so `cd src && PYTHONPATH=. python3 -m tally` fails with `[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'data/sample.ledger'`.",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  }
]
